    location: Situated in the elbow (cubital) joint and fossa of the human body.
      Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Cubital fossa.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Landmark / Feature
    description: triangular anatomical region on the anterior aspect of the elbow,
      bordered by the brachioradialis, pronator teres, and an imaginary line between
      the humeral epicondyles
    function: Provides increased mechanical surface area for muscle and ligament
      anchoring, distributing biomechanical stresses and stabilizing joint mechanics.
    location: Located on the surface of the underlying bone in the elbow (cubital)
      joint and fossa. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
