  - partName: Deltoid region.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: A voluntary skeletal muscle composed of fascicles of striated muscle
      fibers enclosed by the epimysium (Deltoid region). Contraction is mediated
      by somatic motor neurons via the neuromuscular junction.
    function: Generates contractile force to stabilize joints, produce dynamic movement,
      and maintain body posture in the shoulder girdle and pectoral region.
    location: Situated in the muscular compartment of the shoulder girdle and pectoral
      region. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
