  - partName: Body of sternum
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Flat Bone
    description: bone part
    function: Protects underlying thoracic organs (heart, great vessels, trachea);
      forms the anterior anchor for the true ribs (costal cartilages); serves as
      an attachment site for pectoral and abdominal muscles.
    location: Positioned in the anterior midline of the chest wall; articulates with
      the clavicles and the cartilages of ribs 1 through 7. Bilateral or midline
      anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma7487
    fmaPreferredName: Body of sternum
