  - partName: Clavicle.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: The clavicle (collarbone) is an S-shaped, subcutaneous long bone
      bridging the axial skeleton and the upper appendicular skeleton. It is the
      only horizontal long bone in the human skeleton.
    function: Acts as a rigid mechanical strut that suspends the scapula and upper
      limb away from the thoracic wall, maximizing upper extremity range of motion
      and transmitting forces to the axial skeleton.
    location: Spans horizontally across the superior anterior thorax between the
      sternal manubrium medially and the acromion of the scapula laterally. Left
      side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Clavicle.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: plain bone of short length that serves as a strut between the scapula
      and the sternum
    function: Acts as a rigid mechanical strut that suspends the scapula and upper
      limb away from the thoracic wall, maximizing upper extremity range of motion
      and transmitting forces to the axial skeleton.
    location: Spans horizontally across the superior anterior thorax between the
      sternal manubrium medially and the acromion of the scapula laterally. Right
      side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
