  - partName: Femur.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Ligament
    description: lake in British Columbia, Canada
    function: Supports full upper body weight during upright stance and bipedal locomotion;
      transmits ground reaction forces to the pelvis; acts as principal mechanical
      lever for powerful hip and knee musculature.
    location: Situated within the thigh; articulates proximally with the pelvic acetabulum
      (hip joint) and distally with the tibia and patella (knee joint). Left side
      (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Femur.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Ligament
    description: The femur (thigh bone) is the longest, strongest, and heaviest tubular
      long bone in the human body. It consists of a proximal head, neck, greater/lesser
      trochanters, cylindrical shaft, and distal medial/lateral condyles.
    function: Supports full upper body weight during upright stance and bipedal locomotion;
      transmits ground reaction forces to the pelvis; acts as principal mechanical
      lever for powerful hip and knee musculature.
    location: Situated within the thigh; articulates proximally with the pelvic acetabulum
      (hip joint) and distally with the tibia and patella (knee joint). Right side
      (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Fibula.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: The fibula is the slender, lateral bone of the lower leg. It consists
      of a proximal head with an apex, a long slender shaft with muscular attachment
      crests, and a distal expansion known as the lateral malleolus.
    function: Serves as an essential anchor for leg, ankle, and foot muscles, and
      forms the lateral retaining wall (lateral malleolus) of the talocrural mortise
      joint for ankle stability.
    location: Runs parallel and lateral to the tibia in the lower leg, bound to it
      along its length by the interosseous membrane. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Fibula.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: The fibula is the slender, lateral bone of the lower leg. It consists
      of a proximal head with an apex, a long slender shaft with muscular attachment
