  - partName: Humerus.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: The humerus is the major long bone of the upper arm. It features
      a hemispherical proximal head, anatomical/surgical necks, greater/lesser tubercles,
      deltoid tuberosity, spiral groove, and distal capitulum, trochlea, and epicondyles.
    function: Provides rigid structural support for the arm, serves as the skeletal
      lever for shoulder and elbow kinematics, and anchors 24 distinct muscular attachments.
    location: Extends between the shoulder and elbow; articulates proximally with
      the glenoid fossa of the scapula and distally with the radius and ulna. Left
      side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
