  - partName: Lateral process of nasal septal cartilage.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Cartilage
    description: A distinct osseous anatomical landmark and morphological feature
      (Lateral process of nasal septal cartilage) that serves as a site of tendon/ligament
      attachment or articular contact.
    function: Provides increased mechanical surface area for muscle and ligament
      anchoring, distributing biomechanical stresses and stabilizing joint mechanics.
    location: Located on the surface of the underlying bone in the head and cranial
      region. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
