  - partName: Patella.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Sesamoid Bone
    description: The patella (kneecap) is the largest sesamoid bone in the human
      body, embedded within the common tendon of the quadriceps femoris muscle. It
      features a posterior articular cartilage layer up to 6mm thick.
    function: Increases the mechanical lever arm of the quadriceps tendon across
      the knee joint by up to 30%, optimizing knee extension torque while shielding
      the joint from trauma.
    location: Positioned anterior to the distal femur, gliding within the trochlear
      groove (patellar surface) of the femur during knee flexion and extension. Left
      side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Patella.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
