  - partName: Radius.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Ligament
    description: clinical trial
    function: Enables pronation and supination of the forearm by pivoting around
      the ulna, and transmits impact forces from the hand/wrist to the humerus.
    location: Located on the lateral aspect of the forearm; articulates proximally
      with the capitulum of the humerus and radial notch of the ulna, and distally
      with the scaphoid, lunate, and ulna. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Radius.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Ligament
    description: suspension link
    function: Enables pronation and supination of the forearm by pivoting around
      the ulna, and transmits impact forces from the hand/wrist to the humerus.
    location: Located on the lateral aspect of the forearm; articulates proximally
      with the capitulum of the humerus and radial notch of the ulna, and distally
      with the scaphoid, lunate, and ulna. Right side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
