  - partName: Scapula.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Flat Bone
    description: lake in Ontario, Canada
    function: Provides the foundation for shoulder movement through scapulothoracic
      gliding and anchors 17 distinct muscular attachments, including the rotator
      cuff muscles.
    location: Overlies the posterior thoracic ribs 2 through 7; articulates laterally
      with the humerus at the glenohumeral joint and with the clavicle at the acromioclavicular
      joint. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Scapula.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Flat Bone
    description: The scapula (shoulder blade) is a flat, triangular bone located
      on the posterolateral aspect of the thoracic cage. It features a prominent
      spine, acromion, coracoid process, supraspinous/infraspinous fossae, and shallow
      glenoid cavity.
    function: Provides the foundation for shoulder movement through scapulothoracic
      gliding and anchors 17 distinct muscular attachments, including the rotator
      cuff muscles.
    location: Overlies the posterior thoracic ribs 2 through 7; articulates laterally
      with the humerus at the glenohumeral joint and with the clavicle at the acromioclavicular
      joint. Right side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
