  - partName: Tibia.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bursa
    description: The tibia (shin bone) is the large, weight-bearing medial bone of
      the lower leg. It possesses an expanded proximal plateau with medial/lateral
      condyles, a prominent anterior tibial tuberosity, triangular shaft, and distal
      medial malleolus.
    function: Bears approximately 85-90% of the body weight transmitted through the
      lower extremity, enabling stable standing, running, and jumping.
    location: Located anteromedially in the leg; articulates proximally with the
      femoral condyles and distally with the talus and fibula. Left side (bilateral
      structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
