  - partName: Ulna.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: clinical trial
    function: Acts as the rigid axis of the forearm during forearm rotation and provides
      the primary bony constraint for the hinge movement of the elbow joint.
    location: Located on the medial aspect of the forearm parallel to the radius,
      articulating proximally with the trochlea of the humerus and distally with
      the articular disc of the wrist. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: Ulna Length in Black Children
  - partName: Ulna.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: The ulna is the medial, stabilizing long bone of the forearm. Its
      proximal end displays the prominent hook-like olecranon, coronoid process,
      and trochlear notch, tapering distally to a small head with a styloid process.
    function: Acts as the rigid axis of the forearm during forearm rotation and provides
      the primary bony constraint for the hinge movement of the elbow joint.
    location: Located on the medial aspect of the forearm parallel to the radius,
      articulating proximally with the trochlea of the humerus and distally with
      the articular disc of the wrist. Right side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
