    partType: Irregular Bone
    description: A rigid organ of the human skeletal system composed of mineralized
      osseous tissue (compact cortical bone and spongy trabecular bone), periosteum,
      and bone marrow (Vertebra L4).
    function: Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical leverage for movement,
      protective shielding for internal viscera, and hematopoiesis (blood cell generation).
    location: Forms an integral part of the skeletal framework of the vertebral column
      and back. Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
