  - partName: Xiphoid process
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Landmark / Feature
    description: small cartilaginous process (extension) of the lower part of the
      sternum which is usually ossified in the adult human
    function: Provides increased mechanical surface area for muscle and ligament
      anchoring, distributing biomechanical stresses and stabilizing joint mechanics.
    location: Located on the surface of the underlying bone in the human body. Bilateral
      or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma7488
