  - partName: (Abdominal part of pectoralis major muscle).ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscle
    description: A voluntary skeletal muscle composed of fascicles of striated muscle
      fibers enclosed by the epimysium ((Abdominal part of pectoralis major muscle).ol).
      Contraction is mediated by somatic motor neurons via the neuromuscular junction.
    function: Generates contractile force to stabilize joints, produce dynamic movement,
      and maintain body posture in the abdominal cavity.
    location: Situated in the muscular compartment of the abdominal cavity. Bilateral
      or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
