  - partName: Dorsal interossei muscles of hand.o1l
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscle
    description: A voluntary skeletal muscle composed of fascicles of striated muscle
      fibers enclosed by the epimysium (Dorsal interossei muscles of hand.o1l). Contraction
      is mediated by somatic motor neurons via the neuromuscular junction.
    function: Generates contractile force to stabilize joints, produce dynamic movement,
      and maintain body posture in the hand and digits.
    location: Situated in the muscular compartment of the hand and digits. Bilateral
      or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
