  - partName: Lateral head of triceps brachii.ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: The triceps brachii is a powerful three-headed muscle that occupies
      almost the entire posterior compartment of the arm. It arises from the infraglenoid
      tubercle (long head) and posterior humerus (lateral and medial heads), inserting
      onto the olecranon.
    function: Primary and most powerful extensor of the elbow joint; the long head
      also assists in adduction and extension of the humerus at the shoulder joint.
    location: Posterior compartment of the arm; innervated by the radial nerve (C6,
      C7, C8). Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Lateral head of triceps brachii.or
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: The triceps brachii is a powerful three-headed muscle that occupies
      almost the entire posterior compartment of the arm. It arises from the infraglenoid
      tubercle (long head) and posterior humerus (lateral and medial heads), inserting
      onto the olecranon.
    function: Primary and most powerful extensor of the elbow joint; the long head
      also assists in adduction and extension of the humerus at the shoulder joint.
    location: Posterior compartment of the arm; innervated by the radial nerve (C6,
      C7, C8). Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
