  - partName: Long head of biceps brachii.ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: The biceps brachii is a prominent two-headed fusiform muscle located
      on the anterior arm compartment. It arises from the coracoid process (short
      head) and supraglenoid tubercle (long head) and inserts onto the radial tuberosity.
    function: Acts as a powerful supinator of the forearm (especially when flexed)
      and a major flexor of the elbow joint; assists in shoulder flexion and humeral
      head stabilization.
    location: Anterior compartment of the arm; superficial to the brachialis muscle;
      innervated by the musculocutaneous nerve (C5, C6). Bilateral or midline anatomical
      structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Long head of biceps brachii.or
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: The biceps brachii is a prominent two-headed fusiform muscle located
      on the anterior arm compartment. It arises from the coracoid process (short
      head) and supraglenoid tubercle (long head) and inserts onto the radial tuberosity.
    function: Acts as a powerful supinator of the forearm (especially when flexed)
      and a major flexor of the elbow joint; assists in shoulder flexion and humeral
      head stabilization.
    location: Anterior compartment of the arm; superficial to the brachialis muscle;
      innervated by the musculocutaneous nerve (C5, C6). Bilateral or midline anatomical
      structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Long head of biceps femoris.ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: A voluntary skeletal muscle composed of fascicles of striated muscle
      fibers enclosed by the epimysium (Long head of biceps femoris.ol). Contraction
      is mediated by somatic motor neurons via the neuromuscular junction.
    function: Generates contractile force to stabilize joints, produce dynamic movement,
      and maintain body posture in the head and cranial region.
    location: Situated in the muscular compartment of the head and cranial region.
      Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Long head of biceps femoris.or
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: A voluntary skeletal muscle composed of fascicles of striated muscle
      fibers enclosed by the epimysium (Long head of biceps femoris.or). Contraction
      is mediated by somatic motor neurons via the neuromuscular junction.
    function: Generates contractile force to stabilize joints, produce dynamic movement,
      and maintain body posture in the head and cranial region.
    location: Situated in the muscular compartment of the head and cranial region.
      Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Long head of triceps brachii.ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: The triceps brachii is a powerful three-headed muscle that occupies
      almost the entire posterior compartment of the arm. It arises from the infraglenoid
      tubercle (long head) and posterior humerus (lateral and medial heads), inserting
      onto the olecranon.
    function: Primary and most powerful extensor of the elbow joint; the long head
      also assists in adduction and extension of the humerus at the shoulder joint.
    location: Posterior compartment of the arm; innervated by the radial nerve (C6,
      C7, C8). Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Long head of triceps brachii.or
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: The triceps brachii is a powerful three-headed muscle that occupies
      almost the entire posterior compartment of the arm. It arises from the infraglenoid
      tubercle (long head) and posterior humerus (lateral and medial heads), inserting
      onto the olecranon.
    function: Primary and most powerful extensor of the elbow joint; the long head
      also assists in adduction and extension of the humerus at the shoulder joint.
    location: Posterior compartment of the arm; innervated by the radial nerve (C6,
      C7, C8). Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Long plantar ligament.o1l
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Ligament
    description: A dense regular connective tissue band primarily composed of closely
      packed parallel collagen fibers (Long plantar ligament.o1l). Connects adjacent
      osseous structures.
    function: Provides mechanical stability, guides physiological articulation kinematics,
      and prevents excessive or abnormal joint displacement in the foot and toes
      (pedal region).
    location: Spans across the articular capsule and bone margins of the foot and
      toes (pedal region). Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
