  - partName: Longissimus thoracis muscle.e1l
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscle
    description: A voluntary skeletal muscle composed of fascicles of striated muscle
      fibers enclosed by the epimysium (Longissimus thoracis muscle.e1l). Contraction
      is mediated by somatic motor neurons via the neuromuscular junction.
    function: Generates contractile force to stabilize joints, produce dynamic movement,
      and maintain body posture in the human body.
    location: Situated in the muscular compartment of the human body. Bilateral or
      midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
