  - partName: Scapular spinal part of deltoid muscle.ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscle
    description: The deltoid is a large, triangular, multipennate muscle that drapes
      over the glenohumeral shoulder joint. It originates from the lateral third
      of the clavicle, acromion, and scapular spine, converging onto the deltoid
      tuberosity of the humerus.
    function: Primary abductor of the arm beyond 15 degrees (middle fibers); anterior
      fibers flex and medially rotate the arm; posterior fibers extend and laterally
      rotate the arm.
    location: Superficial muscle cap forming the rounded contour of the shoulder;
      innervated by the axillary nerve (C5, C6). Bilateral or midline anatomical
      structure.
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Scapular spinal part of deltoid muscle.or
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscle
