  - partName: Abdominal aorta
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Artery
    description: artery
    function: Carries high-pressure oxygenated blood from the heart to all systemic
      capillary beds via its extensive branching arterial network.
    location: Originates at the base of the left ventricle, arches superiorly and
      posteriorly over the pulmonary trunk, and descends anterior to the vertebral
      column through the thorax into the abdomen. Bilateral or midline anatomical
      structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma3789
    fmaPreferredName: Abdominal aorta
