  - partName: Common hepatic artery
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Artery
    description: An arterial blood vessel carrying oxygenated blood under pressure
      away from the heart to peripheral tissues (Common hepatic artery). Composed
      of tunica intima, media, and adventitia.
    function: Supplies arterial blood, vital oxygen, and nutrients to the muscles,
      organs, and tissues of the abdominal cavity.
    location: Located within the neurovascular compartment of the abdominal cavity.
      Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma14771
    fmaPreferredName: Common hepatic artery
