  - partName: Intrarenal arteries of right kidney
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Artery
    description: The kidney is a bean-shaped retroperitoneal organ with an outer
      renal cortex containing millions of nephrons and an inner renal medulla organized
      into pyramids, draining into minor and major calyces and the renal pelvis.
    function: Filters metabolic waste products (urea, creatinine, uric acid) from
      the blood, regulates fluid/electrolyte balance, maintains acid-base homeostasis,
      controls arterial blood pressure (renin-angiotensin system), and produces erythropoietin.
    location: Retroperitoneal on the posterior abdominal wall, on either side of
      the vertebral column between levels T12 and L3. The right kidney sits slightly
      lower due to the liver. Right side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
