  - partName: Great cardiac vein
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Vein
    description: Cardiac vein, each instance of which is a tributary of some coronary
      sinus situated in some anterior longitudinal sulcus that collects blood from
      the anterior region of some right and left ventricles.
    function: Facilitates systemic venous drainage and cardiovascular circulation
      from the human body back to the central venous system.
    location: Courses through the subcutaneous and deep fascial planes of the human
      body. Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma4707
    fmaPreferredName: Great cardiac vein
  - partName: Inferior vein of left ventricle
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Vein
    description: A venous blood vessel responsible for returning deoxygenated blood
      and metabolic waste products back toward the right atrium of the heart (Inferior
      vein of left ventricle). Contains valves to prevent retrograde flow.
    function: Facilitates systemic venous drainage and cardiovascular circulation
      from the human body back to the central venous system.
    location: Courses through the subcutaneous and deep fascial planes of the human
      body. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
