  - partName: Femoral vein.l
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Vein
    description: A venous blood vessel responsible for returning deoxygenated blood
      and metabolic waste products back toward the right atrium of the heart (Femoral
      vein). Contains valves to prevent retrograde flow.
    function: Facilitates systemic venous drainage and cardiovascular circulation
      from the hip and femoral region back to the central venous system.
    location: Courses through the subcutaneous and deep fascial planes of the hip
      and femoral region. Left side (bilateral structure).
