  - partName: Left renal vein
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Vein
    description: short thick veins which return blood from the kidneys to the vena
      cava
    function: Facilitates systemic venous drainage and cardiovascular circulation
      from the abdominal cavity back to the central venous system.
    location: Courses through the subcutaneous and deep fascial planes of the abdominal
      cavity. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma14336
    fmaPreferredName: Left renal vein
  - partName: Intrarenal veins of left kidney
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Vein
    description: The kidney is a bean-shaped retroperitoneal organ with an outer
      renal cortex containing millions of nephrons and an inner renal medulla organized
      into pyramids, draining into minor and major calyces and the renal pelvis.
    function: Filters metabolic waste products (urea, creatinine, uric acid) from
      the blood, regulates fluid/electrolyte balance, maintains acid-base homeostasis,
      controls arterial blood pressure (renin-angiotensin system), and produces erythropoietin.
    location: Retroperitoneal on the posterior abdominal wall, on either side of
      the vertebral column between levels T12 and L3. The right kidney sits slightly
      lower due to the liver. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Left testicular vein
    systemName: Circulatory System
    partType: Vein
    description: Testicular vein, each instance of which is a tributary of some left
      renal vein that drains some left pampiniform plexus.
    function: Facilitates systemic venous drainage and cardiovascular circulation
      from the human body back to the central venous system.
    location: Courses through the subcutaneous and deep fascial planes of the human
      body. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma14344
    fmaPreferredName: Testicular vein
