    partType: Vein
    description: A venous blood vessel responsible for returning deoxygenated blood
      and metabolic waste products back toward the right atrium of the heart (Inferior
      basal vein of left lung). Contains valves to prevent retrograde flow.
    function: Facilitates systemic venous drainage and cardiovascular circulation
      from the thoracic (chest) cavity back to the central venous system.
    location: Courses through the subcutaneous and deep fascial planes of the thoracic
      (chest) cavity. Left side (bilateral structure).
