  - partName: Liver
    systemName: Visceral System
    partType: Vital Organ
    description: 'Lobular organ, each instance of which has some hepatic lobule as
      its essential morphological unit. Eaxmple: There is only one liver.'
    function: 'Performs over 500 vital metabolic functions: synthesizes bile, plasma
      proteins, and clotting factors; detoxifies endogenous/exogenous compounds;
      metabolizes carbohydrates, lipids, and proteins; stores glycogen and vitamins.'
    location: Occupies the right hypochondriac, epigastric, and part of the left
      hypochondriac regions of the abdomen, immediately beneath the right hemidiaphragm.
      Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
