  - partName: Anterior spinocerebellar tract
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Nervous Tissue
    description: Tract of neuraxis, each instance of which is a a group of nerve
      fibers in the lateral funiculus of the lower thoracic and lumbar segments of
      some spinal cord, arising mostly in the opposite gray matter and ascending
      to some cerebellum by way of the anterior part of the lateral funiculus and
      then the superior cerebellar peduncle; they carry sensory impulses activated
      by nerve endings in somemskin, muscles, tendons, and joints.
    function: Defines spatial boundaries, encloses neurovascular bundles, and provides
      anatomical landmarks for physical examination and surgical approaches.
    location: Situated in the human body of the human body. Bilateral or midline
      anatomical structure.
