  - partName: Motor nucleus of facial nerve.l
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Nerve
    description: A peripheral neural trunk composed of bundled motor, sensory, and
      autonomic axon fibers encased in endoneurium, perineurium, and epineurium (Motor
      nucleus of facial nerve).
    function: Conducts electrical action potentials; delivers motor innervation to
      local muscles and transmits sensory feedback (pain, touch, proprioception)
      from the human body to the CNS.
    location: Courses along the neurovascular pathway of the human body. Left side
      (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
