  - partName: Rubrospinal tract
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Nervous Tissue
    description: Tract of brain, each instance of which is a group of nerve fibers
      in the lateral funiculus of some spinal cord, arising in the large cells of
      the red nucleus of some mesencephalon and terminating predominantly in the
      cervical region of some spinal cord.
    function: Defines spatial boundaries, encloses neurovascular bundles, and provides
      anatomical landmarks for physical examination and surgical approaches.
    location: Situated in the vertebral column and back of the human body. Bilateral
      or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma73877
    fmaPreferredName: Right rubrospinal tract
  - partName: Sciatic nerve.l
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Nerve
    description: The sciatic nerve is the largest and thickest single peripheral
      nerve in the human body (up to 2cm in diameter). Originating from the sacral
      plexus (L4-S3), it bifurcates in the popliteal fossa into the tibial and common
      fibular nerves.
    function: Provides motor innervation to the posterior thigh muscles (hamstrings),
      all lower leg and foot muscles, and sensory innervation to the posteroinferior
      leg, entire foot, and sole.
    location: Emerges through the greater sciatic foramen inferior to the piriformis
      muscle, descending deep to the gluteus maximus down the posterior thigh. Left
      side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
