      autonomic axon fibers encased in endoneurium, perineurium, and epineurium (Common
      fibular nerve).
    function: Conducts electrical action potentials; delivers motor innervation to
      local muscles and transmits sensory feedback (pain, touch, proprioception)
      from the lower leg (crural region) to the CNS.
    location: Courses along the neurovascular pathway of the lower leg (crural region).
      Left side (bilateral structure).
