  - partName: Vagus nerve (X).l
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Nerve
    description: The vagus nerve (Cranial Nerve X) is the longest and most widely
      distributed cranial nerve. It contains approximately 80% sensory afferent and
      20% parasympathetic motor efferent fibers.
    function: Carries primary parasympathetic control to the heart (slowing heart
      rate), lungs (bronchoconstriction), and gastrointestinal tract (stimulating
      peristalsis and acid secretion); innervates laryngeal muscles for phonation.
    location: Exits the skull via the jugular foramen, courses down the neck in the
      carotid sheath, enters the thorax, and distributes to abdominal organs through
      the esophageal hiatus. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
