  - partName: Anterior longitudinal ligament
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Ligament
    description: Ligament of vertebral column, each instance of which is fibrous
      band attached to the ventral surfaces of the bodies of some vertebrae; it extends
      from some occipital bone and the anterior tubercle of some atlas down to some
      sacrum.
    function: Provides mechanical stability, guides physiological articulation kinematics,
      and prevents excessive or abnormal joint displacement in the human body.
    location: Spans across the articular capsule and bone margins of the human body.
      Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma31893
    fmaPreferredName: Anterior longitudinal ligament
  - partName: Anterior meniscotibial ligament (Lateral meniscus).l
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Ligament
    description: A dense regular connective tissue band primarily composed of closely
      packed parallel collagen fibers (Anterior meniscotibial ligament (Lateral meniscus).l).
      Connects adjacent osseous structures.
    function: Provides mechanical stability, guides physiological articulation kinematics,
      and prevents excessive or abnormal joint displacement in the knee joint and
      popliteal fossa.
