    partType: Joint
    description: An anatomical articulation where two or more skeletal bones converge
      (Articular disc of acromioclavicular joint). Typically characterized by an
      articular capsule, synovial membrane, and hyaline cartilage.
    function: Permits controlled mechanical degrees of freedom (flexion, extension,
      rotation, or gliding) while withstanding biomechanical compression and load
      transmission.
    location: Located at the junction between articulating bones in the shoulder
      girdle and pectoral region. Left side (bilateral structure).
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
