  - partName: Intra-articular ligament of head of rib
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Ligament
    description: A dense regular connective tissue band primarily composed of closely
      packed parallel collagen fibers (Intra articular ligament of head of rib).
      Connects adjacent osseous structures.
    function: Provides mechanical stability, guides physiological articulation kinematics,
      and prevents excessive or abnormal joint displacement in the head and cranial
      region.
    location: Spans across the articular capsule and bone margins of the head and
      cranial region. Bilateral or midline anatomical structure.
    fmaId: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma8962
    fmaPreferredName: Intra-articular ligament of head of rib
  - partName: Ischiofemoral ligament.l
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Ligament
