  - partName: Lateral meniscus.l
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Cartilage
    description: A recognized anatomical landmark and topographical region of the
      human body (Lateral meniscus), serving as an important clinical, surgical,
      and anatomical reference point.
    function: Defines spatial boundaries, encloses neurovascular bundles, and provides
      anatomical landmarks for physical examination and surgical approaches.
    location: Situated in the knee joint and popliteal fossa of the human body. Left
      side (bilateral structure).
