  - partName: Oblique popliteal ligament.l
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Ligament
    description: ligament on the back of the knee
    function: Provides mechanical stability, guides physiological articulation kinematics,
      and prevents excessive or abnormal joint displacement in the knee joint and
      popliteal fossa.
    location: Spans across the articular capsule and bone margins of the knee joint
      and popliteal fossa. Left side (bilateral structure).
