  - partName: Palmar capitohamate ligament.l
    systemName: Joints
    partType: Ligament
    description: A dense regular connective tissue band primarily composed of closely
      packed parallel collagen fibers (Palmar capitohamate ligament). Connects adjacent
      osseous structures.
    function: Provides mechanical stability, guides physiological articulation kinematics,
      and prevents excessive or abnormal joint displacement in the hand and digits.
    location: Spans across the articular capsule and bone margins of the hand and
      digits. Left side (bilateral structure).
